two prompts, two calls
  judging    You judge how hard something is. You do not decide whether it works.
  resolving  You say what changes in a world after something has already worked.
  and the resolving call may name only these, which the engine carries out:
    open   target=#<id>           -- a shut thing comes open
    shut   target=#<id>           -- an open thing falls shut
    move   target=#<id> to=(<x>, <z>) -- a thing is shoved, at most 4.0 units, onto ground that carries it
    spill  target=#<id>           -- everything inside an open thing ends up on the ground beside it

